Hi Andrew,

I'm running 2.6.16-rc1 + your driver from mm4.  The entire mm4 patch
causes the kernel to not compile for my ia64 platform.

I'm observing a system hang at shutdown.  Some dpc threads appear to
be in the state below and the associated scsi_wq threads are all as shown.
Smells like a deadlock.

It appears as though the four patches you referenced in email are already
applied.

Have I got the right code?

--

Additional testing also showed an OOPS (below) with the same code.
I was running lots of i/o and did switchdisable / switchenable.

Mike


